# Study Game — React conventions

- Use **functional components** and hooks (`useState`, `useCallback`, `useMemo`, `useEffect` only when needed).
- Keep **game state** in dedicated hooks under `src/hooks/`; avoid prop-drilling more than two levels — lift or use a small context if needed.
- **File names:** `PascalCase.jsx` for components, `camelCase.js` for hooks and utilities.
- **Styling:** Prefer `src/styles/global.css` and co-located class names; no CSS-in-JS unless already introduced.
- **Data:** Read prep content from `src/data/questions.json` (generated by the parser). Do not hardcode large question strings in components.
- **Accessibility:** Interactive elements must be keyboard-focusable; use `<button type="button">` for actions, label icon-only buttons with `aria-label`.
- **Copy:** Keep UI text concise; align tone with ADM interview prep (plain English, actionable).
